<p>The FBI is investigating whether Joe Kent, who resigned this week as director of the US National Counterterrorism Center, improperly shared classified information before leaving office. Multiple outlets said the inquiry began before Kent submitted his resignation on Tuesday, when he told President Trump he could not support the ongoing war in Iran and argued that Iran posed no imminent threat to the United States. The news adds another layer of tension to a widening debate in Washington over the US role in the Iran conflict. Several reports say Kent&#x27;s resignation letter challenged the rationale for the war and accused Israeli officials and media figures of helping build support for military action, while others focus on the FBI&#x27;s leak inquiry and the Justice Department&#x27;s broader scrutiny of people seen as political opponents of President Trump. The case now sits at the intersection of national security secrecy, internal dissent, and a high-stakes foreign policy dispute.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/X8k7k4zzJLuAnSCtbYYlGkWx44JU5olLHfqKn8Vp5rMYHZZefufTTm76dOjIn0e91HU08WY-HRrFnW2hXAZfdkKDGAWa-Afa8-US4FT4FNvNhoUerNtg5EKo2cOQIYT0CrMHbsV2MQZQqa24mmuTqO2KSkXkKp6W-2BJDUgr5mjggzKxSZ3dUD7Dnj1UACOceActUQ2cCOYrdBmh0sVSbYEY3gP4JNNI2CTgUiiAZdPW7LlMPw81X3Kp' alt='Joseph Kent appears before a Senate Committee on Intelligence hearing for his pending confirmation to be director of the National Counterterrorism Center, on Capitol Hill, April 9, 2025, in Washington.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Source depth: AllSides, citing Semafor, said four people with direct knowledge described the matter as a leak investigation centered on allegations that classified information was shared improperly.</li><li>Letter wording: RT reported that Kent wrote that high-ranking Israeli officials and influential American media figures mounted a misinformation campaign that undermined Trump&#x27;s position and helped lead the US into war.</li><li>Source sensitivity: SCMP said the account of the FBI probe came from a person who requested anonymity because the inquiry is ongoing.</li><li>Senate trail: Le Monde said Kent&#x27;s path to the NCTC post included an April 9, 2025, Senate Intelligence Committee confirmation hearing.</li></ul><blockquote>I could not in good conscience support the ongoing war in Iran. - Joe Kent</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Joe Kent: Kent&#x27;s resignation letter argued that Iran did not pose an imminent threat to the United States and said he could not continue to back the war under those conditions. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c33j3gxvgmro'>BBC News</a>)</li><li>FBI investigators: Investigators are examining whether Kent improperly shared classified information, according to people familiar with the matter cited in several reports. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3347098/fbi-investigating-top-us-security-official-who-resigned-over-iran-war'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>Trump administration allies and pro-Israel commentators: RT reported that some administration allies and pro-Israel commentators have tried to portray Kent as a leaker and as hostile to Israel after his resignation letter became public. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/news/635535-kent-resignation-fbi-investigation/'>RT</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/03/19/fbi-probing-counterterrorism-official-who-quit-over-iran-war-us-media-reports_6751597_4.html'>FBI probing counterterrorism official who quit over Iran war, US media reports</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/635535-kent-resignation-fbi-investigation/'>Why is the FBI investigating a former counterterrorism chief who opposes the US-Israeli war on Iran?</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3347098/fbi-investigating-top-us-security-official-who-resigned-over-iran-war'>FBI ‘inves